Impact:
Bank Indonesia Regulation No. 17/3/PBI/2015
- Article 2(2): Explicitly states that all payment transactions and financial obligations in Indonesia must be settled in Rupiah. It includes transactions using credit cards, debit cards, ATM cards, and other electronic payment systems.
- Article 4: The obligation to use Rupiah as referred to in Article 2 paragraph does not apply to the following transactions:
a. certain transactions in the context of implementing the state revenue and expenditure budget;
b. d. receipt or provision of grants from or to foreign countries;
c. international trade transactions; 
deposits in banks in the form of foreign currency; or
e. international financing transactions.

